<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> Baptism as the sacrament of new birth in Christ, the gateway to the Christian life.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that Baptism is the "door of the sacraments" and necessary for salvation.</li>
<li>Discover the Old Testament figures (Flood, Red Sea) that prefigure Baptism.</li>
<li>Learn the matter, form, minister, and effects of the sacrament.</li>
<li>Understand how Baptism removes original sin and restores sanctifying grace.</li>
<li>Embrace the dignity of being a child of God and live from that identity.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> <em>&laquo;Go therefore and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit&raquo;</em> (Mt 28:19)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 1210-1284</p>

</section>

